<title>RUSSIA: Yeltsin names new head of Russia's Vneshekonombank.</title>
<headline>Yeltsin names new head of Russia's Vneshekonombank.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian President Boris Yeltsin has appointed Andrei Kostin as chairman of Vneshekonombank, a presidential press official said on Friday.</p>
<p>Vneshekonombank replaced the Soviet foreign trade bank of the same name and services Russia's foreign debts, inherited from the former Soviet Union. It also distributes payments for MinFin bonds.</p>
<p>Kostin was previously first deputy chairman of National Reserve Bank.</p>
</text>
